#import "../lib.typ": *

#section(
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(119)

    #instruction[Write thirty-five to forty H's and "Hauling" fifteen times in 60 seconds.]
  ], lines: 6, examples: ("drill-119", "drill-119-2")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(120)

    Pupils should not lose sight of the fact that motion determines form. Take
    care of the motion and the forms of the letters will develop easily and
    naturally. A careful study of the movement as applied to capital K will be
    helpful. After making the first part of the letter, the hand (with the pen
    in the air) should swing below the base line, describing an oval and
    returning upward to the beginning point of the last part of the letter. Be
    sure to connect the parts with a loop, as shown in the copy. Drop the
    finishing part below the base line. Don't forget the word practice.

    #instruction[Write forty K's and "Killing" twelve times in 60 seconds.]
  ], lines: 6, examples: ("drill-120", "drill-120-2")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(121)

    Some pupils will be able to write the word at higher speed and still do
    good work.

    #instruction[Write fifty to sixty P's and "Pulling" twelve times in 60 seconds.]
  ], lines: 6, slots: 2, examples: ("drill-121", "drill-121-2")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(122)

    Be sure to fix in mind the image of the letter before attempting it. Study
    closely the proportions and the direction of every stroke.

    Do not forget that your advancement depends upon movement, and that
    movement depends much upon position. The body should be self-supporting,
    with the feet resting squarely on the floor, and should not crowd against
    the desk; the right arm should be well out from the side; the right hand
    well in front of the eyes; and the paper twelve or fourteen inches from
    the eyes.

    If the wrist or side of the hand rests on the paper, all motion coming
    from the muscles of the arm will stop at the wrist and it will be an
    impossibility to use muscular movement. Watch the wrist and the side of
    the hand closely. Remember that the propelling power is above the elbow,
    in the upper arm and shoulder.

    Write line after line of the word "Running" with a light, quick motion,
    and compare with the copy frequently.

    #instruction[Write fifty R's and "Running" twelve to fourteen times in 60 seconds.]
  ], lines: 6, examples: ("drill-122", "drill-122-2")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(123)

    Turn to lesson fifty-four and practice and study capital S in accordance
    with the instructions. Enough time should be reserved to write at least
    one page of the word "Swelling".
  ], lines: 6, examples: ("drill-123", "drill-123-2")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(124)

    Pupils who cannot make good loop letters should make a special study of
    lesson thirty-two.
  ], lines: 6, examples: ("drill-124", "drill-124-2")),
)
